1
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:49,591
What?

2
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:52,677
We…

3
00:00:53,178 --> 00:00:54,888
Why are we here?

4
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:57,974
We evacuated here
because of the typhoon, right?

5
00:00:58,058 --> 00:01:01,186
But who brought us all the way here?

6
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:02,395
What is this place?

7
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:04,689
-Where are we?
-Huh? What?

8
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:10,487
It's a shrine!

9
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:11,654
-A shrine?
-What?

10
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:13,156
Thank you for having us.

11
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:19,037
Huh?

12
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:21,998
Whoa! Look at this!

13
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,249
What?

14
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:28,755
A large-scale landslide
has occurred in Tatsumi Town.

15
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:32,634
Many local houses
were caught up in the landslide,

16
00:01:32,717 --> 00:01:34,719
but there have been no casualties.

17
00:01:36,304 --> 00:01:38,890
-Is this where the villa was?
-Yeah.

18
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:40,725
The villa is gone!

19
00:01:40,809 --> 00:01:44,354
The road is over there,
so the villa was completely washed away!

20
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:47,524
-This is the orange garden!
-You're right!

21
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:48,983
Wait a minute.

22
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:51,402
If we had stayed there,
we would have died.

23
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:54,864
Yeah. If we hadn't left the villa
back then, by now, we would be…

24
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:56,032
Hey!

25
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:57,617
My grandma's ashes!

26
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:02,205
-Grandma, the villa is gone!
-Grandma…

27
00:02:02,288 --> 00:02:03,206
They brought her…

28
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:07,210
Is God telling us
that our vacation is over?

29
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:08,461
God?

30
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:11,631
What kind of god
would cause a disaster like this?

31
00:02:11,714 --> 00:02:12,590
True.

32
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:15,969
Yeah, no god or Buddha
would do something like this!

33
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:21,683
What kind of god helped us…

34
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,894
Everyone, let's calm down!

35
00:02:24,978 --> 00:02:29,607
Come on. It's a shame that the villa
is gone, but we all survived!

36
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:33,111
The land remains.
I will make it big as an actor…

37
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:36,239
I'll rebuild
a Konta villa there in no time!

38
00:02:36,322 --> 00:02:38,366
Then we can all have a barbecue again!

39
00:02:38,449 --> 00:02:40,535
-Konta!
-Oh, Rinrin!

40
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:41,578
Oh, sorry, Rinrin!

41
00:02:55,216 --> 00:02:57,176
TWO DAYS LATER

42
00:02:59,053 --> 00:03:02,223
Well, our vacation was forced to an end.

43
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:03,600
Shall we get to work?

44
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:06,060
No other choice…

45
00:03:06,936 --> 00:03:09,480
Everyone has to work after all.

46
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:12,358
You can't survive without money.

47
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:14,652
My savings ran out,
so I'll get a part-time job.

48
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:18,239
I should also register
at a new temp agency.

49
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:21,451
I need to find a new job.

50
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:23,494
I will work too.

51
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:27,206
Well, our long summer vacation is over.

52
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:29,042
Do your best with the movie.

53
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:30,919
Yeah, leave it to me.

54
00:03:31,002 --> 00:03:32,128
I'll do my best.

55
00:03:32,629 --> 00:03:33,546
Come on, everyone!

56
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:36,883
-What?
-Back to society! Let's go!

57
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:40,053
Be quiet! You're bothering
the other customers.

58
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:42,138
-I'm sorry.
-Cut it out!

59
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:46,976
Tetsuro. Stop paying with cash.

60
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:49,270
-Here, use this to pay.
-Got it.

61
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:50,188
See you all!

62
00:03:50,271 --> 00:03:52,023
-See you.
-I'll send you the money!

63
00:03:52,106 --> 00:03:53,524
-Okay.
-Bye, Midori. See you later!

64
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:55,652
-See you!
-I'll be in touch, Konta.

65
00:03:57,028 --> 00:03:58,238
Please!

66
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:02,951
She's too cute.

67
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,245
Excuse me!

68
00:04:11,709 --> 00:04:13,503
Dad? Hello, what's wrong?

69
00:04:15,463 --> 00:04:16,839
Disaster insurance?

70
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:18,591
Oh, right.

71
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:21,135
You're going to the government office
to do the paperwork?

72
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:22,679
I see.

73
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:23,846
Okay, thank you.

74
00:04:24,472 --> 00:04:27,558
For now,
I'll take Grandma's urn to my place.

75
00:04:27,642 --> 00:04:28,476
Yeah.

76
00:04:28,559 --> 00:04:29,394
Okay.

77
00:04:29,477 --> 00:04:30,895
Dad, I'm here too!

78
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:32,272
Sorry, I hung up.

79
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:33,439
Never mind.

80
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:36,651
Oh, it's my manager.

81
00:04:38,569 --> 00:04:39,737
Hello?

82
00:04:39,821 --> 00:04:40,863
Yes, I've been well.

83
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:44,158
Oh, yes. I'm in Tokyo right now.

84
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:46,577
Huh? Seriously?

85
00:04:47,745 --> 00:04:49,080
Yes, I'll be there.

86
00:04:49,163 --> 00:04:51,582
I'll head over right now. Yes, okay.

87
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:52,667
I understand.

88
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:55,128
I'll do my best. Excuse me.

89
00:04:56,421 --> 00:04:57,380
-Oh, man.
-Huh?

90
00:04:57,463 --> 00:05:00,008
I got a role. A late-night drama.
And I have lines!

91
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:02,093
Oh, that's great!

92
00:05:02,176 --> 00:05:04,721
As I thought, Tokyo was waiting for me.

93
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:07,432
Well, I'm off. They're already shooting.

94
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:09,058
-Take care.
-All right. Um…

95
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:11,686
As for the money, Midori, you pay.

96
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:15,732
Thank you!

97
00:05:31,122 --> 00:05:32,749
Why is this spot empty?

98
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:52,101
I need to move forward too.

99
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:00,735
Thank you very much.

100
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:05,073
ORANGE PEELS 500 YEN

101
00:06:11,829 --> 00:06:12,789
These too, please.

102
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:14,415
Certainly.

103
00:06:20,129 --> 00:06:22,381
You've done something terrible.

104
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:27,011
I'm sorry.

105
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:31,265
I erased those humans' memories.

106
00:06:31,349 --> 00:06:33,935
No one remembers you anymore.

107
00:06:34,852 --> 00:06:40,399
Your human form has become grains of sand,
turned into sea foam,

108
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:41,901
and vanished.

109
00:06:44,987 --> 00:06:45,947
However!

110
00:06:46,572 --> 00:06:47,490
However!

111
00:06:49,951 --> 00:06:51,619
The Dragon God

112
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:54,705
has headhunted you.

113
00:06:55,581 --> 00:06:56,541
What?

114
00:06:57,291 --> 00:06:59,168
Japan is a land of gods.

115
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:03,172
And the shrines that have existed there
since ancient times

116
00:07:03,756 --> 00:07:07,677
operate on different values
compared to us.

117
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:15,059
My reason for existing
was to witness the demise of humans.

118
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:18,062
To see them delivered to the underworld.

119
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:19,230
But…

120
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:27,822
I lost sight of my duties as Grim Reaper.

121
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:31,492
And ended up saving their lives.

122
00:07:33,161 --> 00:07:34,662
Why did it come to this?

123
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:38,291
It was an unprecedented act of misconduct.

124
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,962
Why did you have to cause such trouble?

125
00:07:43,045 --> 00:07:45,131
I want to know the reason.

126
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:48,676
Why?

127
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:58,895
Because I was on vacation.

128
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:10,072
I've often been told that vacations
change a person's way of thinking.

129
00:08:10,865 --> 00:08:13,659
But to think it would
even affect a Grim Reaper…

130
00:08:14,410 --> 00:08:15,244
Well…

131
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:18,164
As a result, for better or worse,

132
00:08:18,247 --> 00:08:21,959
that god, the Dragon, has recruited you.

133
00:08:28,799 --> 00:08:31,928
Those gods over there, unlike us,

134
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:35,056
have been helping humans
since ancient times.

135
00:08:35,139 --> 00:08:37,058
It's like their main job.

136
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:42,104
Even a soft-hearted, good-for-nothing
Grim Reaper like you

137
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:46,067
might have some potential,
from their point of view.

138
00:08:46,859 --> 00:08:48,236
You are the man they need…

139
00:08:48,819 --> 00:08:49,654
No,

140
00:08:50,488 --> 00:08:52,573
the god they need.

141
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:54,617
Something like that.

142
00:08:58,079 --> 00:08:59,872
So…

143
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:02,833
If I become a god of a shrine,

144
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:06,379
are you going to revive me again?

145
00:09:08,047 --> 00:09:09,882
Don't get ahead of yourself.

146
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:12,468
You won't become a god right away.

147
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:16,055
First, you must do decades
of community service.

148
00:09:16,138 --> 00:09:19,809
No, in this case, earthly service.

149
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:25,356
You will reflect on your transgression,
while working in their world.

150
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:50,715
You only get one shot.

151
00:09:51,382 --> 00:09:53,009
There are no redos.

152
00:09:53,801 --> 00:09:56,220
If you hit the sea, that's where you go.

153
00:10:13,237 --> 00:10:14,614
Nice throw.

154
00:10:15,281 --> 00:10:17,158
Some fine control right there.

155
00:10:38,554 --> 00:10:39,722
-Midori.
-Yes?

156
00:10:39,805 --> 00:10:41,098
Do you want some coffee?

157
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:42,850
Oh, not right now.

158
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:43,893
Okay.

159
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:04,705
Hello, Konta?

160
00:11:05,206 --> 00:11:06,707
How is the shoot going?

161
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:09,085
Period dramas must be tough, huh?

162
00:11:09,168 --> 00:11:12,880
It's about the Great Tenpo famine,

163
00:11:12,963 --> 00:11:15,132
so it seems I have to lose weight.

164
00:11:15,216 --> 00:11:17,968
The director banned me from having lunch.

165
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:18,969
So…

166
00:11:19,053 --> 00:11:20,304
I'm eating leaves for real!

167
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:24,392
In order to survive…

168
00:11:25,309 --> 00:11:28,562
you even have to eat grass!

169
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:40,658
THE GREAT TENPO FAMINE

170
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:42,743
SHOOTING IS GOING SMOOTHLY!

171
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:47,998
Also, Rinrin is like,
incredibly busy with work.

172
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:50,084
We can't really meet up.

173
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:51,252
I see.

174
00:11:51,335 --> 00:11:54,338
Both of you are working so hard,
it's admirable.

175
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:55,256
Admirable?

176
00:11:56,507 --> 00:11:57,883
Wait, what about you, Midori?

177
00:11:57,967 --> 00:11:59,301
What have you been up to?

178
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:01,220
Me?

179
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:03,264
Well, I…

180
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:12,982
There you go.

181
00:12:13,065 --> 00:12:14,859
Summer oranges!

182
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:21,699
Konta.

183
00:12:21,782 --> 00:12:23,868
Konta, do your best!

184
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:26,495
Until you make it big, I will work too!

185
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:31,041
In order to rebuild that villa,
you must become famous!

186
00:12:31,625 --> 00:12:32,501
Yeah!

187
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:35,421
Rinrin, I'll do my best.

188
00:12:36,046 --> 00:12:39,008
For your sake, and to rebuild that villa,

189
00:12:39,633 --> 00:12:41,760
I'll risk my life to play this role!

190
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:45,347
Oh, sorry. Are you rolling? Sorry.

191
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:47,099
Oh, it's not a private call.

192
00:12:47,641 --> 00:12:49,226
A utility company called.

193
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:50,519
Sorry, I'm so sorry.

194
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:54,398
I got scolded! I did!

195
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:55,608
Sorry, I'm sorry.

196
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:00,988
ONE YEAR LATER

197
00:13:20,299 --> 00:13:22,510
It has been a year
since that vacation at the villa,

198
00:13:22,593 --> 00:13:25,971
and the environment surrounding us
has changed a lot.

199
00:13:32,728 --> 00:13:36,106
My brother is finally starting to be
recognized as an actor,

200
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:38,901
and little by little,
work has started coming in.

201
00:13:40,110 --> 00:13:43,030
The man with the slicked-back hair
in Yama-chan,

202
00:13:43,113 --> 00:13:45,616
played by Konta Hoshino, is coming in!

203
00:13:46,659 --> 00:13:48,994
Shall I slick your hair back?

204
00:13:49,578 --> 00:13:51,622
-Good morning.
-Morning.

205
00:13:51,705 --> 00:13:54,625
Rinrin is still working
at the supermarket.

206
00:13:55,417 --> 00:13:56,752
-Oh, Manager.
-Good morning.

207
00:13:56,835 --> 00:13:58,128
-Good morning.
-Do your best today.

208
00:13:58,212 --> 00:13:59,672
I will!

209
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:05,386
Tsumugi started a part-time gig
doing tarot readings at a theme park.

210
00:14:05,469 --> 00:14:09,348
Seems she got pretty good reviews,
so she's been doing this six days a week.

211
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:13,269
The tarot will reveal
all about your destiny!

212
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:15,896
Here goes!

213
00:14:18,023 --> 00:14:20,109
You are not suited for business.

214
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:21,819
Give it up.

215
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:23,737
Seriously?

216
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:29,743
Tetsuro rarely contacts us,

217
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:33,038
but it seems he is working
at a campsite with a fishing pond.

218
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:39,420
By the way, Tetsuro also came up
with the title of the essay I am writing.

219
00:14:44,925 --> 00:14:48,721
TAKING APPLICATIONS!
BIANNUAL ESSAY CONTEST

220
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:53,058
As you can see,
I started writing an illustrated essay.

221
00:14:54,018 --> 00:14:56,061
I'm using that summer as material.

222
00:14:56,645 --> 00:15:00,858
I wanted to leave a record
of the orange recipes from that villa.

223
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:05,154
Not as a smartphone video,
or a social media post,

224
00:15:05,237 --> 00:15:06,572
but with my own hands.

225
00:15:08,324 --> 00:15:10,534
As a kid, I drew terrible manga.

226
00:15:11,118 --> 00:15:13,412
I haven't improved much since then,

227
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:17,750
but I feel like if I don't draw it,
I won't be able to move on.

228
00:15:32,222 --> 00:15:35,851
I wish I had taken a picture of that sea.

229
00:17:23,834 --> 00:17:25,252
A swallowtail butterfly.

230
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:12,716
Hey!

231
00:18:19,389 --> 00:18:20,432
You dropped this.

232
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:22,684
A large summer orange.

233
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:27,564
You… can have it.

234
00:18:28,148 --> 00:18:28,982
What?

235
00:18:29,691 --> 00:18:32,653
Hello, Ms. Midori.

236
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,281
Hey.

237
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:44,998
Is there anywhere nice around here?

238
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:54,466
I came here to have a vacation.

239
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:04,685
Vacation…

240
00:19:53,692 --> 00:19:56,236
THE VACATION PRINCIPLE

241
00:19:56,320 --> 00:20:02,743
MY SUMMER ORANGE RECIPES
BY MIDORI HOSHINO

242
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:30,015
A VACATION FOR LIFE

243
00:22:30,098 --> 00:22:31,767
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
